From: Project Luma <maintainers@projectluma.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve explicit build-host Go parallelism

After the GC-budget patch, also preserve explicit Go scheduler concurrency
through Soong's env-i boundary. Ninja job count alone does not constrain the
Go graph compiler. This tunes the build host, not Android application policy.
Pinned Soong/AOSP Apache-2.0 copyright and source notices remain intact.

--- a/ui/build/soong.go
+++ b/ui/build/soong.go
@@ -169,6 +169,9 @@
 	invocationEnv := make(map[string]string)
 	if gc := os.Getenv("GOGC"); gc != "" {
 		invocationEnv["GOGC"] = gc
+	}
+	if parallel := os.Getenv("GOMAXPROCS"); parallel != "" {
+		invocationEnv["GOMAXPROCS"] = parallel
 	}
 	debugMode := os.Getenv("SOONG_DELVE") != ""
 
